The  login accounting service module for PAM provides functional‐
ity for only one PAM category: session management.  In  terms  of
the parameter, this is the feature.  The login accounting session
management component provides functions to initiate and terminate
sessions.  The function records the session in the and databases.
The  function  does nothing.  The following options may be passed
to the authentication module:  debugging  information  at  level.
Don’t update records or print messages if the user is i.e. logged
in on the same tty on top of another user.  suppress warning mes‐
sages  to  the  user.   Ignore I/O failures.  The module and this
manual page were developed for the Project by ThinkSec AS and NAI
Labs, the Security Research Division of Network Associates,  Inc.
under DARPA/SPAWAR contract N66001‐01‐C‐8035 as part of the DARPA
CHATS research program.
